{% comment %}
  Site-owned include (no upstream counterpart).

  Fine-tuning for the about-page profile photo. Upstream gives the floated
  profile `width: 30%` and `margin-left: 1rem` and nothing else, so the photo's
  top sits a few pixels above the first line of the intro paragraph, and the
  circular crop makes the right-hand whitespace read as larger than the left
  even though the box is flush with the content edge.

  Only applies from 576px up; below that the profile is full width and stacks,
  where a negative margin would risk horizontal overflow.
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  @media (min-width: 576px) {
    .profile.float-right {
      /* A little more breathing room between the text and the photo, and a small
         nudge right so the circle's visual edge lines up with the page margin. */
      margin-left: 1.75rem;
      margin-right: -0.5rem;
    }

    /* Drop the photo so its top aligns with the first line of the intro text
       rather than the top of the paragraph box. */
    .profile figure {
      margin-top: 0.4rem;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
